From 6db1ead4982a8c5bba1949a5523bc36b6fa184ab Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Alessandro Fontana <alessandro.fontana@pm.me>
Date: Fri, 6 Nov 2026 15:46:24 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] libcamera: software_isp: Clamp defective pixels

Without an ISP nothing hides the defective pixels of the sensor, and the
demosaicing turns each into a coloured dot, the more visible the higher
the gain. Limit every pixel of 16-bit formats to the range of its four
nearest neighbours of the same colour, plus a margin that grows with the
signal, in the copy of the frame the threaded path works on.

On the SR259 of the Galaxy Tab A 10.1 the dots fixed over six preview
frames go from 41 to 0 per Mpx, at the same 28.6 fps and sharpness.

Assisted-by: LLM
Signed-off-by: Alessandro Fontana <alessandro.fontana@pm.me>
